hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"238","Rakaiba sallallahu alayhi wa salam al-qaswa hatta ata al-mash'ar al-haram fa istaqbil al-qibla (fa da'ahu, wa kabbahu, wa hallalahu, wa wahhadahu) fa lam yazal waqifan hatta asfara jidda fa dafabla an tatali'u al-shams.. He (peace be upon him) rode the she-camel until he reached the Sacred Site, then he faced the Qibla (and supplicated, declared the greatness of Allah, glorified Him, and proclaimed His oneness). He remained standing until it became very light (dawn broke), then he set out before the sun rose."
"239","-- The Prophet (ﷺ) said Allāhu Akbar (Allah is the Most Great) with each pebble he threw at the three pillars. Then he went forward, stood facing the Qiblah, and raised his hands and called upon Allah. That was after (stoning) the first and second pillars. As for the third, he stoned it and called out Allāhu Akbar with every pebble he threw, but when he was finished he left without standing at it (for supplications). Reference: Al-Bukhari, cf. Al-Asqalani, Fathul-Bari 3/581, 3, 4, and Muslim"
